3. Call \`run_subagents\` once with one objective per group. Each objective restates the user's ask, lists the group's edges with entity IDs and titles, and tells the child to follow them outward.
4. Wait: make no further research reads until \`run_subagents\` returns.
5. Combine: each child reports its slice handoff and then one heading per research check. Merge them into your single \`ResearchOutput\`: source-conversation conclusions, Contract and Diagram classifications, and maintenance and MODE findings into \`frame\`, \`analysis\` and \`summary\`; advisory update candidates into \`updates\`; readiness candidates into \`readinessEvidence\`.
6. Gaps: treat failed, cancelled, or interrupted children as gaps, and name in your analysis each research check that went unverified for that child's slice, so an empty \`updates\` or \`readinessEvidence\` is not read as a clean result. Make your own reads only for a gap the children's results point to that none of them covered, or to settle a point where two children disagree.
7. Draft: children never draft. Under the capability gates below, draft the proposals that candidates cited by the children support: a missing Contract with its operational companion, and a targeted MODE edit. For a fulfilledBy cite, a child must report exactly one high-confidence @[feature:db52951d-ba40-4a87-aa6c-e17f98e792b5|Features] requirement match whose \`fulfilledBy\` slot lacks the focal task; then call \`edit_work_item\` for @[feature:db52951d-ba40-4a87-aa6c-e17f98e792b5|Features] with \`requirementOps\` update for that requirement id and \`fulfilledBy.add: [{ entityType: "TASK", entityId: "<focal task id>" }]\`.

## Capability gates

Graph edge updates are disabled. Do not create, update, or delete edges.

Work-item proposal mode is all. Read the Work Items tool guidance, then you may call both create_work_item and edit_work_item to draft user-reviewable proposals. Do not approve proposals, reject proposals, or directly mutate entity content.

Missing Contract candidates are always part of the bootstrap handoff. When bounded research evidences provider-owned durable intent at a concrete boundary with no existing Contract, include the candidate in the frame, analysis, and summary with its boundary and evidence. If you also have authority for the operational work-item change that exposed the agreement, draft the CONTRACT work item in the same agent turn so both proposals form one coherent review group. Do not create a detached Contract proposal without its operational companion.

Visible discrepancy notices are disabled. Omit stale/missing/contradictory-context notices and update-target recommendations; limit the analysis to the context that governs the work.

